; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Truchet Tiles
; CATEGORY: Patterns & Mandalas
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     tiles, random, arcs, grid, emergence
; SUMMARY:  Covers the screen with square tiles, each holding two quarter circles turned one of two ways at random.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Every tile has the same simple drawing: two quarter circles in
;   opposite corners. A coin toss decides whether the tile is turned
;   or not. Because the arcs always meet the edges at the middle of
;   each side, they join up with their neighbors, and long winding
;   paths and closed loops appear all over the screen. The color
;   changes slowly from the bottom row to the top.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Run it again for a different maze of curves.
;   Change TILE to make the tiles bigger or smaller.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * ARC with a heading: the arc starts at the turtle's heading and
;     sweeps clockwise
;   * RANDOM 2 as a coin toss
;   * why matching edges make tiles join up
;   * a simple rule plus randomness can make a complex picture
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use (RANDOM 4) = 0 instead of a fair coin. What changes?
;   * Turn tiles by a rule instead of chance, for example when
;     row + column is even.
;   * Use diagonal lines instead of arcs (the original Truchet tile).
; ============================================================

make "tile 50

; A tile whose bottom left corner is at (x, y).
; Way 0: arcs round the bottom left and top right corners.
; Way 1: arcs round the top left and bottom right corners.
; Each arc is a quarter circle of radius TILE / 2 centered on a corner.
to truchet :x :y :way
  ifelse :way = 0 [
    corner :x :y 0
    corner :x + :tile :y + :tile 180
  ] [
    corner :x :y + :tile 90
    corner :x + :tile :y 270
  ]
end

; Stand on a corner, face along one edge, and sweep 90 degrees.
to corner :x :y :heading
  penup setxy :x :y setheading :heading
  pendown arc 90 :tile / 2
end

to cover
  for [row 0 11] [
    ; mix from teal at the bottom to pink at the top
    setpencolor (list 80 + 14 * :row 220 - 10 * :row 210 - 2 * :row)
    for [col 0 15] [
      truchet -400 + :col * :tile -300 + :row * :tile random 2
    ]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [20 40 60]
setpensize 6
cover
